preConditionHook:
// The largest COUNTERTREND body of the last lookback bars is smaller than
// bodyMultiple times the average WITH-trend body over the same window: no
// outsized bear bar has shown up in the bull move yet. Place it negated for
// Brooks's 'larger bear bars are appearing', a two-sidedness warning.
//
// An extreme against a mean, which is what keeps it apart from both dominance
// rules (they compare two sums) and from BodyAboveAverageMultiple (which sizes
// the CURRENT bar against a mean).
//
// Non-qualifying bars contribute ZERO rather than being skipped, so both
// window statistics stay defined over a fixed denominator of lookback bars.
// The clamp is a plain if against a running 0, NOT MaxList(x, 0): MaxList is
// ACCEPTED only for selection among tick-grid PRICE operands and a body is a
// computed difference -- the same call BarOverlapFraction and
// ConsecutiveBarsLittleOverlap make.
//
// The averages are never divided out. 'max < K * sum / N' is written
// 'max * N < K * sum', so the rule cannot raise EL's runtime divide-by-zero on
// a degenerate lookback, and both twins evaluate the identical product form.
//
// Every scratch value is a declared local rather than a hook-scope
// declaration, so a second placement of this rule gets its own prefixed copy,
// and all of them are reset at the top of the hook. Deepest bar read is
// lookback - 1.
maxDownBody = 0.0;
maxUpBody = 0.0;
sumUpBody = 0.0;
sumDownBody = 0.0;
for (kk = 0; kk < (int)lookback; ++kk) {
    upBody = 0.0;
    if (el_gt(close[kk], open[kk])) upBody = close[kk] - open[kk];
    dnBody = 0.0;
    if (el_lt(close[kk], open[kk])) dnBody = open[kk] - close[kk];
    if (el_gt(upBody, maxUpBody)) maxUpBody = upBody;
    if (el_gt(dnBody, maxDownBody)) maxDownBody = dnBody;
    sumUpBody = sumUpBody + upBody;
    sumDownBody = sumDownBody + dnBody;
}
